From 61c9f6788673e5f54673a5e3280e15ce56c4dfbe Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Kristian <kristian@apache.org>
Date: Sat, 24 Oct 2026 01:46:36 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] Support Confluent protobuf without licensed JARs

The Confluent table description supplier supported PROTOBUF subjects
only after kafka-protobuf-provider and kafka-protobuf-types, which are
under the Confluent Community License, were copied into the plugin
directory by hand.

Build protobuf descriptors from schema text with the Wire parser and
protobuf-java linking in trino-record-decoder, and register a Trino
owned schema provider for PROTOBUF schemas that resolves references
through the schema registry client. Decode records with the schema id
and message indexes of their Confluent wire format frame, and map the
table columns to writer fields by field number against the schema the
table was described with. Map a table to the message its subject
names under the RecordNameStrategy and TopicRecordNameStrategy.

Support INSERT into Confluent protobuf tables, encoding rows with the
table's schema in the Confluent wire format, and add authentication
and TLS configuration for the schema registry client, which now
verifies the registry host name by default.
